  "design_section": "7.19",
  "design_notes": [
    "Section title: \"Capsule/payload recovery (returning missions)\". The table has no number at all. The \"Fact\" column is stored in twin; propulsive landing shows none. F18 is the fact-bank entry for the Orion parachutes.",
    "Propulsive landing \"new tech\" is stored as maturity new, as for the engines whose drawback reads \"new tech\". \"Proven\" (splashdown) stays a strength text, as in the other part files. The design gives no reliability for the band to apply to.",
    "Vote step 3 of 6.2 is \"Payload return (capsule contracts: heat shield, recovery)\", so the options list the capsule contracts C3, C4 and C6, like the heat shields.",
    "\"Needs pusher escape engines\" is requires_part les_integrated_pusher (7.4 says the pusher engines enable propulsive landing upgrades). The escape system is offered only in C4 and C6 (escape_system.json), so propulsive landing lists C4 and C6 and not the uncrewed C3.",
    "The two parachute options carry parachute_failure with the drop test as mitigation (8.4) and enable MG-23 Parachute Sequence. MG-27 Recovery Team is \"F13 splashdown\", so only the splashdown option enables it.",
    "\"Recovery ship needed\", \"salt water\", \"rockets must fire at the right height\", \"precise\" and \"reusable\" have no numbers; they are flags.",
    "C0 requires parachute recovery of a non-capsule payload, but section 6.2 gives C0 no recovery vote (see contracts.json), so C0 is not listed. C8 lands a booster, not its payload."
  ],
